<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- The bundled Python sidecar loads dylibs from python.org builds, which
       carry a DIFFERENT Team ID than ours. Under the hardened runtime the
       loader refuses those by default and the sidecar dies at startup, so
       notarization fails on a binary that never ran. This entitlement is
       applied ONLY to the sidecar entrypoint (see packaging/build_dmg.sh) —
       never to the app itself, which needs no such exemption.

       NOT referenced from tauri.conf.json's macOS.entitlements: putting it
       there makes Tauri apply it to the .app as well, which measurably did
       happen (dumping the built app's entitlements showed the exemption).
       The Tauri binary loads no dylibs from another Team ID, so that only
       weakens the app's signature for nothing. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
